CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
found no match for symbol 'power'
--
Regression for overload resolution among multiple converting
constructors per [over.match.best].

Previously cpp_typecheck_conversions::user_defined_conversion_sequence
returned false on the first non-unique viable candidate, even
when one candidate was strictly better-ranked.  That caused
calls like

    BigInt power(const BigInt&, const BigInt&);
    power(2, size_t{});

to be rejected with

    found no match for symbol 'power'

despite `BigInt(int)` being an exact match for the int argument
and `BigInt(unsigned long)` being an exact match for the size_t
argument.  Fixed by tracking the best rank seen so far and
flagging ambiguity only on a tie at the best rank.
